FINAL ANSWER:
The bus factor of `lib/` is **1**. If Troy Goode leaves, nobody is left who knows most of the code.

`lib/` is a single file, `lib/index.js` (238 lines). It's the package's `main` entry point, so all of the CORS middleware lives there. With only one file, I ran the git history and blame commands myself and skipped the skill's contributor-analyzer agent step.

## 🚌 Bus Factor Analysis: `lib/`
Period: all history (2013-01-30 → 2026-04-12) | Generated: 2026-10-24

### Bus Factor: 1

> If Troy Goode left, about two-thirds of `lib/` would have no author who still knows it. The next largest contributor wrote 9% of the lines and hasn't touched the file since 2017.

### The raw numbers are misleading at first

A plain `git blame` says **Fiona Formatter owns 214 of 238 lines (90%)**. That comes from a single commit, `62628c0`, which only changed indentation and quote style. Troy's latest commit, `b2005d9`, only added `// checked` comments to 12 lines. Neither commit adds real understanding of the code, so I re-ran blame with both ignored (`-w -M -C --ignore-rev`). I also merged two names that share the same email (Alejandro Caravaca Puchades and alex94puchades).

| Author | Lines (blame, cosmetic commits ignored) | Share | Commits | Last real change to lib |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode | 157 | **66%** | 29 | 2016-08-23 |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 22 | 9% | 4 | 2017-10-04 |
| Alejandro Caravaca Puchades | 16 | 7% | 5 | 2015-05-28 |
| Raymond Feng | 9 | 4% | 1 | 2015-01-13 |
| 15 others | ≤6 each | ~14% | 1–3 each | 2013–2021 |

### Overview

| Metric | Value |
|---|---|
| Source files in `lib/` | 1 |
| Files with bus factor 1 | 1 (100%) |
| Critical single-owner files | 1 |
| Total contributors ever | 24 |
| Last real logic change | 2021-07-20 (LuisEGR) |

### Critical Risk Areas

| File | Main owner | Owner active? | Dependents | Risk |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `lib/index.js` | Troy Goode (66%) | ⚠️ Committed 2026-04-10, but only comments. Last real change 2016 | Package entry point; all 5 test files; every downstream user | **[CRITICAL]** |

### Knowledge Heat Map
```
lib/
└── index.js  [███████░░░] 🔴 Bus Factor: 1 (Troy Goode 66%, next is 9%)
```

### Why this matters more than the number suggests
- **Nobody really knows this code anymore.** No one has made a real logic change to `lib/` in over five years. Even Troy's own detailed knowledge may be stale.
- **The repo is active, just not here.** Recent commits from people like Jon Church, Ulises Gascón and Phillip Barta in 2026 are docs, release and CI work. They are the people most likely to pick up `lib/`, but blame shows none of them have changed its logic.
- **The file is small (238 lines), so this is fixable.** The risk is high, but the effort to fix it is low.

### Recommendations
1. **Immediate:** Have one of the current maintainers write down how `configureOrigin`, `isOriginAllowed` and the preflight handling work, ideally reviewed by Troy. This alone could take the bus factor to 2.
2. **Short-term:** Add a `.git-blame-ignore-revs` file listing `62628c0` and `b2005d9`. Then `git blame` and GitHub's blame view will show who actually wrote each line, not the formatter.
3. **Ongoing:** Route the next real `lib/` change, such as a bug fix or option, to someone other than Troy, with Troy as reviewer.

